WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:05.576
About three hundred thousand years ago, in Africa, people like us began.

2
00:00:05.833 --> 00:00:09.530
Later, they met other humans: Neanderthals.

3
00:00:09.530 --> 00:00:13.167
Many people outside Africa still carry a small trace of them.

4
00:00:13.417 --> 00:00:18.875
Some walked out of Africa, along coastlines, toward the lands we now call South Asia.

5
00:00:19.125 --> 00:00:22.833
They pressed their hands to stone, as if to say: we were here.

6
00:00:23.083 --> 00:00:26.016
Around fires, they told stories.

7
00:00:26.016 --> 00:00:29.500
Every lesson, every name, passed from mouth to ear.

8
00:00:29.750 --> 00:00:31.833
They planted seeds, and stayed.

9
00:00:32.083 --> 00:00:34.458
They built cities beside great rivers.

10
00:00:34.708 --> 00:00:39.625
On our coast, ships came for pepper and spice, and the old songs travelled on.

11
00:00:39.875 --> 00:00:43.750
Grandmother to grandchild. Thousands of generations.

12
00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:48.252
For three hundred thousand years, we kept our stories by mouth.

13
00:00:48.252 --> 00:00:49.701
Most of them are lost.

14
00:00:50.833 --> 00:00:54.026
[Example voice] “Mole, listen to this…”

15
00:00:54.326 --> 00:00:57.409
Every one of them was someone's Muthassi.

16
00:00:57.409 --> 00:01:00.376
Now, every family can keep the voices.

17
00:01:00.708 --> 00:01:06.040
Your story is the newest leaf on a tree three hundred thousand years old. Keep it.

18
00:01:06.875 --> 00:01:09.503
Kin. Join the waitlist.

